msgid ""
"**Warning**   \n"
"This program is [**experimental**](../../development/experimental-"
"features.md#xp-feature-nix-command) and its interface is subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:6
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:8
msgid ""
"`nix store roots-daemon` - run a daemon that returns garbage collector roots "
"on request"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:10
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:12
msgid "`nix store roots-daemon` \\[_option_...\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:14
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:16
msgid "Run the daemon:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:22
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:24
msgid ""
"This command runs a daemon that serves garbage collector roots from a Unix "
"domain socket. It is not required in all Nix installations, but is useful "
"when the main Nix daemon is not running as root and therefore cannot find "
"runtime roots by scanning `/proc`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:28
msgid ""
"When the garbage collector runs with [`use-roots-daemon`](../../store/types/"
"local-store.md#store-local-store-use-roots-daemon) enabled, it connects to "
"this daemon to discover additional roots that should not be collected."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:31
msgid ""
"The daemon listens on [`<state-dir>`](../../store/types/local-store.md#store-"
"local-store-state)`/gc-roots-socket/socket` (typically `/nix/var/nix/gc-"
"roots-socket/socket`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:33
msgid "Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:35
msgid ""
"The protocol is simple. For each client-initiated Unix socket connection, "
"the server:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:38
msgid ""
"Sends zero or more [store paths](../../store/store-path.md) as NUL-"
"terminated (`\\0`) strings."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:39
msgid "Closes the connection."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:41
msgid "Example (with `\\0` shown as newlines for clarity):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:47
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:49
msgid ""
"No information is provided as to which processes are opening which store "
"paths. While only the main Nix daemon needs to use this daemon, any user "
"able to talk to the main Nix daemon can already obtain the same information "
"with [`nix-store --gc --print-roots`](../../command-ref/nix-store/gc.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:52
msgid ""
"Therefore, restricting this daemon to only accept the Nix daemon as a client "
"is, while recommended for defense-in-depth reasons, strictly speaking not "
"reducing what information can be extracted versus merely restricting this "
"daemon to accept connections from any [allowed user](../../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-allowed-users)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:54
msgid "Systemd socket activation"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-roots-daemon.md:56
msgid ""
"`nix store roots-daemon` supports systemd socket-based activation, [just "
"like `nix daemon`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md#systemd-socket-"
"activation)."
msgstr ""

